diff --git a/packages/coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md b/packages/coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md
--- a/packages/coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,18 @@
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Synara isolated native Expert patch
+
+- Adds seven private ACP lifecycle methods for host-bound target profiles, durable native Task identity/outbox, started acknowledgement before child execution, per-child cancellation and request-time Gateway credentials. Skills, context and MCP identity replace rather than merge parent capabilities; ordinary native Tasks keep their existing scheduler and AgentSession.
+- The host supplies `_meta.synaraNativeTask = {parentGeneration,parentTurnId,targetAgentNames}` on an authorized prompt after the compiled-build capability check. Child ownership is captured at the actual tool call, not at delayed background launch. Final native Task scheduling fixes private `deliveryMode` in prepare and durable recovery: inline results return natively without a second host continuation; async output remains inspectable but only the host's durable terminal owner may automatically continue the parent. Expert speculative admission waits for final scheduling; ordinary Tasks retain speculation.
+- Fixed Expert parents retain `task.maxRecursionDepth: 0`. After private ACP prompt metadata arrives, builtin reconciliation exposes Task only for the verified opaque targets; the depth exception requires an admitted, captured parent tool call for that exact target and generation. Ordinary/unscoped children remain blocked, and withdrawn metadata, cancellation, stale generations, unsupported preparation and invalid target profiles never fall back to ordinary Task execution. Previously admitted async children keep their captured ownership across a natural turn boundary.
+- The private capabilities handshake may bind one canonical, connection-owned `catalogDirectory` before sessions open. Only its `agents/*.md` definitions participate in Task discovery, ahead of ambient names and independently of `omp-plugins`; the root never enters extension/plugin discovery or loads sibling code, hooks, skills, scripts or MCP. No-directory ACP/probes stay valid but do not advertise native targets. Captured native targets missing from their catalogue fail closed. Create-time, reload and in-flight discovery isolate catalogue roots and bridge lifetimes; complete target resources still come only from the prepared profile.
+- Native admission captures the real Task call synchronously in the SDK's before-call hook, before its first await; delayed `tool_execution_start` observations cannot race admission or rewrite its scope. Internal lookups use the durable SDK session identity without changing the ACP protocol parent ID. Temporary native Task output remains owned until the bridge reads the complete terminal summary, then follows the original cleanup/async/isolation retention policy.
+- Interrupted native Expert sessions are transcript-only until explicit host reconciliation: parent resume and query never restart them. Nonterminal records without a live native execution return `not-found`, which the host must treat as unknown, not permission to redispatch. Immutable terminal events remain queryable/retriable.
+- MCP discovery is disabled during child session creation; only a durable started ACK permits target MCP initialization and fresh per-HTTP-request credentials. Initialization completes before the child prompt; no ACK/credential/eager-initialization cycle is introduced.
+- Native Expert children receive the essential, read-only `native_expert_report_artifacts` tool. It declares the exact deliverable relative paths once, including shell/eval/hashline-edit outputs. The in-process executor supplies the actual SDK root, including isolated workspaces; the runtime safely reads real bytes, computes SHA-256/size, and synchronously copies those bytes into the host-issued per-attempt `profile.artifactRoot` before the original isolation cleanup. Terminal delivery checks this captured version, never a removed or mutable workspace. Completed production runs must explicitly report files or `[]`; budgets, traversal, links and staging overwrites fail closed. The host independently verifies and preserves immutable FileResourceStore byte versions, without granting filesystem authority from a Provider path. Ordinary Task result modes, models, credentials and isolation lifecycle are unchanged.
+- Source runs refuse the capability handshake until the isolated builder embeds verified source/patch/toolchain provenance. This patch is not a daily-binary installation, release or runtime acceptance claim.
+
